{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789231418,"nonce":"kOM5EetpQf42V7AL9jZZE+z5v+U=","title":"drop_insert frees a box an extern retained","message":"`ModuleFacts::build` records every function's pointer parameters as\nborrowed, externs included, because the lowering gives a pointer\nparameter `Borrowed` ownership by default. A host function declared\n`extern def set(c: Cell, v: Any)` that stores the box it is handed\ntherefore looks like a borrower, and the pass frees the box right\nafter the call:\n\n    %v5 = call sym \"zyntax_box_i64\"(%val)\n    call @host_signal_cell_set(%v4, %v5)\n    call sym \"zyntax_box_free\"(%v5)      // the host still points at it\n\nReproducer: crates/zynml/tests/signal_cell_any.rs,\na_scalar_round_trips_through_an_any_cell (reads back 0). It surfaced\nwhen Any became a pointer type in HIR; before that the parameter was\nan i64 the pass could not see as a pointer at all.\n\nFix: the pass knows nothing about what a host does with a pointer, so\nan extern's parameters count as borrowed only when the symbol is one\nthe pass classifies as borrowing (the `zyntax_box_get_*` readers, and\nthe IO, String and Math plugin families, which read their arguments\nand return fresh storage). Any other extern is an escape.","files":null}]}